\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}Standard number systems are $\mathbb N,\mathbb Z,\mathbb Q,\mathbb R,\mathbb C$. Specialized notation and index ranges follow the cited source and the definitions below.


A $k$-CNF function is the Boolean function computed by a conjunction of clauses of width at most $k$. Distinct functions are counted separately from distinct formulas; a unate function becomes monotone after fixed negations of selected input coordinates.
